{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-72792","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-135079","text":"Graphonomous FAQ"}]},{"id":"blk-72793","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-135080","text":"This page answers the most common questions about Graphonomous, its MCP interface, and operating model."}]},{"id":"blk-72794","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-135081","text":"What is Graphonomous?"}]},{"id":"blk-72795","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-135082","text":"Graphonomous is a continual-learning memory engine for AI agents. It stores knowledge as a graph, supports confidence-updating feedback loops, and exposes all capabilities through MCP tools/resources."}]},{"id":"blk-72796","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-135083","text":"Does Graphonomous retrain model weights?"}]},{"id":"blk-72797","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-135084","text":"No. Graphonomous does "},{"id":"spn-135085","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-135086","text":" retrain model weights. Learning happens in the memory graph by storing knowledge and updating confidence based on outcomes."}]},{"id":"blk-72798","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-135087","text":"What problem does it solve?"}]},{"id":"blk-72799","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-135088","text":"It gives agents durable, evolving memory and better decision quality over time by combining:"}]},{"id":"blk-72800","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-72802","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-135089","text":"semantic retrieval"}]}],"id":"blk-72801","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-72804","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-135090","text":"graph neighborhood expansion"}]}],"id":"blk-72803","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-72806","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-135091","text":"causal outcome feedback"}]}],"id":"blk-72805","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-72808","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-135092","text":"goal tracking"}]}],"id":"blk